{"answerArea":{"calculator":true,"chi2Table":false,"periodicTable":false,"tTable":false,"zTable":false},"hints":[{"content":"Let's try to find the limit using direct substitution.","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}},{"content":"$\\begin{align}\n\\displaystyle\\lim_{x\\to 2}\\dfrac{x+2}{x-2}\u0026=\\dfrac{2+2}{2-2}\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=\\dfrac{4}{0}\n\\end{align}$\n\nOur expression evaluates to a nonzero number over zero. In such cases, the limit **doesn't exist**.","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}},{"content":"In conclusion, $\\displaystyle\\lim_{x\\to 2}\\dfrac{x+2}{x-2}$ doesn't exist.","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}}],"itemDataVersion":{"major":0,"minor":1},"question":{"content":"**Find $\\displaystyle\\lim_{x\\to 2}\\dfrac{x+2}{x-2}$.**\n\n[[☃ radio 1]]\n\n","images":{},"widgets":{"radio 1":{"alignment":"default","graded":true,"options":{"choices":[{"content":"$4$","correct":false},{"content":"$1$","correct":false},{"content":"$0$","correct":false,"isNoneOfTheAbove":false},{"content":"The limit doesn't exist","correct":true,"isNoneOfTheAbove":false}],"deselectEnabled":false,"displayCount":null,"hasNoneOfTheAbove":false,"multipleSelect":false,"randomize":false},"static":false,"type":"radio","version":{"major":1,"minor":0}}}}}
